    "Ethiopia": ["Ethiopia","Africa",1,"🇪🇹","Addis Ababa","126M","1.10M km²","Horn of Africa","Ethiopia","Addis_Ababa","Rock-Hewn_Churches,_Lalibela","Lalibela Rock Churches & Simien Highlands","Populous highland nation in the Horn of Africa, source of the Blue Nile","Africa's oldest independent nation and the birthplace of Arabica coffee, Ethiopia rises on a massive volcanic plateau split by the Great Rift Valley—giving birth to the Blue Nile at Lake Tana. Its capital Addis Ababa hosts the African Union, while Lalibela preserves 12th-century rock-hewn churches.","Never colonized, this Horn of Africa highland giant is the birthplace of Arabica coffee, source of the Blue Nile, and home to the rock-hewn churches of Lalibela.",["silk","extreme"],"Tropical Highland"],
