    "Madagascar": ["Madagascar","Africa",1,"🇲🇬","Antananarivo","30M","587K km²","Indian Ocean","Madagascar","Antananarivo","Avenue_of_the_Baobabs","Avenue of the Baobabs & Lemurs","World's fourth-largest island, separated from southeastern Africa by the Mozambique Channel","Separated from mainland Africa and India over 88 million years ago, the world's fourth-largest island evolved as an 'eighth continent' of biodiversity: over 90% of its wildlife—including all wild lemurs and six giant baobab species—exists nowhere else on Earth.","The world's fourth-largest island lies off southeastern Africa across the Mozambique Channel, where over 90% of wildlife—including all wild lemurs and towering baobabs—is endemic.",["extreme","ports"],"Tropical Savanna"],
    "Mexico": ["Mexico","Americas",1,"🇲🇽","Mexico City","129M","1.96M km²","North America","Mexico","Mexico_City","Chichen_Itza","Chichén Itzá & Sierra Madre","North American country between the United States and Central America","Linking North and Central America between the Pacific Ocean and Gulf of Mexico, Mexico was the cradle of Olmec, Maya, and Aztec civilizations and is the world's most populous Spanish-speaking nation. Its biodiversity spans Sonoran deserts, volcanic highlands, and Yucatán cenotes.","The world's most populous Spanish-speaking country bridges the Pacific and Caribbean-Atlantic gulf, cradling ancient Aztec and Maya wonders like Chichén Itzá and Teotihuacán.",["silk","ports"],"Subtropical Highland"],
    "Macedonia": ["North Macedonia","Europe",3,"🇲🇰","Skopje","1.8M","26K km²","Balkans","North_Macedonia","Skopje","Lake_Ohrid","Ancient Lake Ohrid & Canyon Matka","Landlocked Balkan republic directly north of Greece and west of Bulgaria","Set in the central Balkans directly north of Greece, North Macedonia is a mountainous country crowned by Lake Ohrid—one of Europe's oldest and deepest tectonic lakes, harboring unique endemic species and medieval lakeside monasteries. Its capital Skopje bridges Roman, Byzantine, and Ottoman eras.","Directly north of Greece in the mountainous Balkans, this landlocked republic shares ancient tectonic Lake Ohrid, one of Europe's oldest and deepest lakes.",[],"Continental"],
    "Mali": ["Mali","Africa",2,"🇲🇱","Bamako","23M","1.24M km²","West Africa","Mali","Bamako","Timbuktu","Timbuktu & Great Mosque of Djenné","Large landlocked West African Sahara-Sahel country crossed by the Niger River","Home to the medieval West African empires of Ghana, Songhai, and Mali—whose legendary king Mansa Musa made Timbuktu a renowned center of Saharan gold trade and Islamic scholarship—this vast nation spans the dry Sahara north to the fertile inner delta of the Niger River.","Crossed by the upper Niger River across the Sahara and Sahel, this landlocked West African nation preserves legendary Timbuktu and the Great Mud Mosque of Djenné.",["silk","extreme"],"Arid Desert"],
