    "Malaysia": ["Malaysia","Asia",1,"🇲🇾","Kuala Lumpur","34M","330K km²","Southeast Asia","Malaysia","Kuala_Lumpur","Petronas_Towers","Petronas Towers & Borneo Kinabalu","Southeast Asian nation split between the Malay Peninsula and northern Borneo","Split across the South China Sea between the populous Malay Peninsula—bordering the vital Strait of Malacca—and biodiverse Sarawak and Sabah on Borneo, Malaysia pairs the towering Petronas Twin Towers in Kuala Lumpur with 130-million-year-old rainforests and 4,095-meter Mount Kinabalu.","Divided by the South China Sea between a mainland peninsula on the Strait of Malacca and northern Borneo, this nation pairs the Petronas Towers with towering Mount Kinabalu.",["ports"],"Tropical Rainforest"],
    "Namibia": ["Namibia","Africa",2,"🇳🇦","Windhoek","2.6M","826K km²","Southern Africa","Namibia","Windhoek","Sossusvlei","Sossusvlei Red Dunes & Skeleton Coast","Arid South Atlantic nation northwest of South Africa, home to the world's oldest desert","Named for the coastal Namib—believed to be Earth's oldest desert—where towering apricot sand dunes crash straight into the cold Benguela Current along the misty Skeleton Coast. Despite its sparse population, Namibia protects vast wildlife reserves including Etosha Pan and Fish River Canyon.","Bordering the South Atlantic north of South Africa, this sparsely populated nation holds the misty Skeleton Coast and towering red dunes of Sossusvlei in Earth's oldest desert.",["extreme"],"Arid Desert"],
    "New Caledonia": ["New Caledonia","Oceania",3,"🇳🇨","Nouméa","270K","18.6K km²","Melanesia","New_Caledonia","Noum%C3%A9a","New_Caledonia_Barrier_Reef","World's Largest Coral Lagoon","South Pacific French archipelago east of Australia with a massive coral lagoon","Located in the Coral Sea 1,200 km east of Australia, this special collectivity of France surrounds its main island Grande Terre with one of the planet's largest barrier reefs and coral lagoons. Its ancient Gondwanan soils hold roughly a quarter of the world's nickel reserves.","Floating in the Coral Sea east of Australia, this French Pacific archipelago boasts one of Earth's largest UNESCO coral lagoons and huge nickel reserves.",["ports"],"Tropical Savanna"],
